Indices: 012345.
Black cells at 5. Wait, $s[0]='W', s[1]='B', s[2]='W', s[3]='W', s[4]='W', s[5]='B'$.
Black cells at indices 1 and 5.
First black cell is at 1.
Greedy strategy: place interval starting at 1. Interval covers $[1, 1+3-1] = [1, 3]$.
Cells covered: indices 1, 2, 3.
Is index 1 covered? Yes.
Is index 5 covered? No.
Next uncovered black cell is at 5.
Place interval starting at 5. Interval covers $[5, 5+3-1] = [5, 7]$.
Cells covered: 5, 6, 7.
Since $n=6$, index 7 is out of bounds, but that's fine, we just care about covering black cells.
